{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdgiPBWF4n1th9RML7Y9VT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found and read all the key files you requested. Here's a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Files Found and Read\n\n### 1. Main Experiment Plan\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThis is the full experiment plan with 15+ experiments spanning three main claims about code execution simulation. Key experiments include:\n- **cwm-baseline**: Compare CWM generation vs classification\n- **multi-seed-core**: Multi-seed validation for statistical significance\n- **trace-then-judge**: Chain-of-thought ablation\n- **model-size-scaling**: 4B to 8B scaling analysis\n- **diagnostic-rerepair**: Downstream application to repair agents\n- **oracle-f2p-stratified**: Oracle analysis stratified by test count\n- **repo-level-training**: SWE-bench dataset experiments\n\n### 2. \"Worst\" Tier Scenario Details\n**Files**: Two comprehensive worst-case scenario files:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260511T214810/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260511T231719/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n\n**Key worst-tier narrative**:\n- **Claim 1 fails**: CWM generation gap ≤4 F1 vs classification at function-level; reformulation advantage not fundamental\n- **Claim 2 fails**: Per-test diagnostic precision insufficient; re-repair lift ~0.5% (not significant)\n- **Claim 3 salvageable**: Oracle frontier becomes negative characterization—per-test advantage theory only holds under rare conditions (T≥2, block-correlated errors)\n- **Pivot direction**: Reframe as analysis/negative-result paper targeting ICSE 2027 empirical study track or EMNLP Findings\n\n**Worst scenario predicted results**:\n- CWM 4B: 84.3-85.1 F1 (vs cls 87.1-87.9) — gap ~2.8pp, statistically insignificant\n- Trace-then-Judge: -1.9pp at 4B (vs direct cls), but +0.7pp at 8B — confounded with model capacity\n- Traj-level vs per-test: only 0.9pp difference, drowned in noise\n- Per-test precision/recall: 71% precision, 65% recall for failures — insufficient for reliable diagnostics\n- Oracle weighted advantage (iid): only 0.035pp (vs 0.075pp block-correlated) — almost no practical value\n\n### 3. Phase and Scenario Files\n\n**Phase 1 logs** found in dream reports:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_*/logs/phase1_attempt0.log`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_*/logs/phase2_{best,median,worst}_attempt0.log`\n\n**Structured worst-tier data** in JSON format:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260511T214810/worst/experiment_data.json`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260511T231719/worst/experiment_data.json`\n\n## Key Worst-Tier Findings Summary\n\nThe worst scenario includes detailed expected results for 13 experiments showing:\n\n1. **Equivalence at scale**: Both 4B and 8B show classification ≈ generation with parallel scaling curves\n2. **Negligible downstream impact**: Diagnostic re-repair gains only 0.5pp (1 additional resolved instance out of 200)\n3. **Error structure near i.i.d.**: Measured correlation 0.08 vs block-simulation 0.45, undermining oracle block-correlated assumptions\n4. **T=1 dominance problem**: 68.7% of instances have only 1 failing test, making per-test granularity mathematically equivalent to trajectory-level\n5. **Repo-level generalization gap**: 13.7-14.3pp drop from function-level to repo-level, showing methods don't scale beyond toy scenarios\n\nAll files are located in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/` with artifacts in the `artifacts/dream_reports/` subdirectory structure organized by timestamp and scenario tier (best/median/worst)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23fb2834-2812-4457-b569-54861da1d013","uuid":"b9ea754d-ec88-4fcb-b371-045f87d612c9","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:00:53.547Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the project at /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16, find and read the following files:\n1. experiment_plan.yaml or similar (the full experiment plan)\n2. Any file defining the \"worst\" tier scenario details\n3. Any file with \"phase1\" or \"scenario\" or \"tier\" in the name\n\nSearch broadly: check YAML, JSON, and MD files in the root directory and subdirectories like configs/, plans/, scenarios/, etc.","agentId":"a4e9192a14c0acf97","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found and read all the key files you requested. Here's a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Files Found and Read\n\n### 1. Main Experiment Plan\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThis is the full experiment plan with 15+ experiments spanning three main claims about code execution simulation. Key experiments include:\n- **cwm-baseline**: Compare CWM generation vs classification\n- **multi-seed-core**: Multi-seed validation for statistical significance\n- **trace-then-judge**: Chain-of-thought ablation\n- **model-size-scaling**: 4B to 8B scaling analysis\n- **diagnostic-rerepair**: Downstream application to repair agents\n- **oracle-f2p-stratified**: Oracle analysis stratified by test count\n- **repo-level-training**: SWE-bench dataset experiments\n\n### 2. \"Worst\" Tier Scenario Details\n**Files**: Two comprehensive worst-case scenario files:\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-researc