{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011SjQpRy8YcD8739bUcydpR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document of all the findings:\n\n## Summary: Analysis Results from exec-sim-repair-verifier\n\nI've successfully located and analyzed the key research results mentioned in your narrative. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. ERROR COMPLEMENTARITY ANALYSIS (75%/83% Breakdown)\n\n**Source**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/report/paper_materials.md`\n\nThe matched-seed analysis reveals clear complementary error patterns:\n- **CLS dominant error**: Miss bugs (False Negatives) — **75.5% of CLS errors**\n  - Calculation: 178 FN out of 236 total CLS errors = 75.4% ≈ 75.5%\n- **CWM dominant error**: False alarms (False Positives) — **83.1% of CWM errors**\n  - CWM generates incorrect positive predictions in ~83.1% of its error cases\n- This asymmetry in error modes is the foundation for their complementarity as a verification ensemble\n\n**Cross-reference**: Verified in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/report/paper_consistency_audit.md`\n\n---\n\n### 2. ORACLE ENSEMBLE 90.63% RESULT\n\n**Source**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/data/error_overlap_analysis.txt` and `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/data/cls_cwm_error_overlap.md`\n\n**Complete Error Overlap Statistics (seed42, n=1890)**:\n| Category | Count | Percentage |\n|----------|-------|-----------|\n| Both correct | 1601 | 84.71% |\n| CLS-only correct | 59 | 3.12% |\n| CWM-only correct | 53 | 2.80% |\n| Both wrong | 177 | 9.37% |\n\n**Oracle ensemble accuracy: 90.63%**\n- Union correct: 1713 samples\n- Oracle gain over CLS: +2.80pp\n- Oracle gain over CWM: +3.12pp\n- Cohen's Kappa (predictions): 0.88 (strong agreement)\n- Cohen's Kappa (correctness): 0.73\n\n**Per-mutation complementarity**:\n- off_by_one: Most complementary (CWM-only 4.8%, both wrong 14.9%)\n- return_value: Least complementary (96.8% both correct)\n\n---\n\n### 3. MATCHED-SEED-8B-PREDICTIONS EXPERIMENT\n\n**Source**: Checkpoints dated 2026-05-12 at `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/checkpoints/matched-seed-8b-predictions_DONE_20260512T174621.json`\n\n**Experiment Status**: COMPLETED\n- **Hypothesis**: Generate matched-seed per-instance predictions (8B CWM eval JSONs or 4B supplementary analysis) for error overlap/oracle analysis\n- **Available matched CLS-CWM pairs**: 3 pairs (seed0/seed42/seed456)\n  - CWM seed0: 87.57%\n  - CWM seed42: ~87% (established)\n  - CWM seed456: 86.98%\n- **Missing**: CWM seed123/789 and 8B predictions (distributed across cloud infrastructure)\n- **Conclusion**: 3 pairs sufficient for error overlap analysis; foundational for oracle 90.63% result\n\n---\n\n### 4. EFFICIENCY ANALYSIS (1-Token vs N-Token)\n\n**Source**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/data/inference_cost_results_summary.txt` and worker result JSON\n\n**Inference Cost Comparison** (CPU bfloat16, Qwen3-4B + LoRA):\n\n| Metric | Classification (1-token) | CWM Generation (N-token) | Ratio |\n|--------|------------------------|------------------------|-------|\n| Output tokens (mean) | 2.0 | 6.2 | **3.1x** |\n| Latency (mean) | 9,761 ms | 10,612 ms | **1.09x** |\n| Throughput | 0.1024 sps | 0.0942 sps | 0.92x |\n\n**CWM Target Token Distribution** (1890 samples):\n- Mean: 4.7 tokens\n- Median: 5.0 tokens\n- p95: 7 tokens\n- Max: 28 tokens\n\n**Key Efficiency Insights**:\n1. **Token overhead**: CWM outputs 3.1x more tokens than classification\n2. **CPU latency**: Only 1.09x slower due to prefill dominance (input processing ~260 tokens shared across both methods)\n3. **GPU impact**: Differential will be more pronounced on GPU since per-token decode becomes the bottleneck\n4. **Architectural advantage**: CLS produces exactly 1 token regardless of output complexity; CWM scales with output length\n\n---\n\n### 5. ADDITIONAL KEY FINDINGS\n\n**Paper Statistics Summary** (from `paper_materials.md`):\n- **4B Function-Level**: CLS mean 88.43%, CWM mean 87.19% (gap: +1.25pp)\n- **8B Function-Level**: CLS mean 89.40%, CWM mean 86.96% (gap: +2.43pp)\n- **Scaling gap widening**: Gap increases with model size (+1.18pp from 4B to 8B)\n- **Repo-Level Results**: CLS 83.63% vs CWM 58.04% (25.59pp gap)\n  - CWM failure driver: 53.7–67.2% unparseable (token-budget exhaustion, string-value errors)\n\n**Block Correlation & Clustering**:\n- ICC: 0.191 (significant block structure)\n- Design effect: 3.97x (cluster correlation matters)\n- Error clustering observed: 2.81x more all-correct problems than random expectation\n\n**Paper Material Completeness**:\n- Verified against registry: 88.43/87.19 (5-seed), 2.43pp (3-seed 8B), TOST p=0.007, oracle 90.63%, 83.63/58.04 (repo-level)\n- 42–43% parseable, 53.7–67.2% unparseable (repo-level CWM)\n\n---\n\n### File Locations Reference\n\n| Analysis | Primary File |\n|----------|-------------|\n| Error complementarity (75%/83%) | `/artifacts/_project/report/paper_materials.md` (lines 151-155) |\n| Oracle 90.63% detailed breakdown | `/artifacts/_project/data/error_overlap_analysis.txt` |\n| Matched-seed experiment metadata | `/checkpoints/matched-seed-8b-predictions_DONE_20260512T174621.json` |\n| Inference cost comparison | `/artifacts/_project/data/inference_cost_results_summary.txt` |\n| Complete consistency audit | `/artifacts/_project/report/paper_consistency_audit.md` |\n| CLS vs CWM error overlap detailed | `/artifacts/_project/data/cls_cwm_error_overlap.md` |\n\nAll results are from completed experiments between 2026-05-11 and 2026-05-12, verified against the project registry and cross-referenced in multiple audit reports."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23fb2834-2812-4457-b569-54861da1d013","uuid":"9b583c4f-8a3d-4fb6-8574-c2292460ba62","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:02:55.523Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/, search for:\n1. Any analysis of \"error complementarity\" between CLS and CWM (the 75%/83% numbers mentioned in narrative)\n2. The oracle ensemble 90.63% result\n3. Any efficiency analysis (inference cost comparison, 1-token vs N-token)\n4. The \"matched-seed-8b-predictions\" experiment results which may contain CLS/CWM error analysis\n\nCheck artifacts/, analysis files, notebooks, and any recent reports.","agentId":"a2d54394c18ab6515","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document of all the findings:\n\n## Summary: Analysis Results from exec-sim-repair-verifier\n\nI've successfully located and analyzed the key research results mentioned in your narrative. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. ERROR COMPLEMENTARITY ANALYSIS (75%/83% Breakdown)\n\n**Source**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/report/paper_materials.md`\n\nThe matched-seed analysis reveals clear complementary error patterns:\n- **CLS dominant error**: Miss bugs (False Negatives) — **75.5% of CLS errors**\n  - Calculation: 178 FN out of 236 total CLS errors = 75.4% ≈ 75.5%\n- **CWM dominant error**: False alarms (False Positives) — **83.1% of CWM errors**\n  - CWM generates incorrect positive predictions in ~83.1% of its error cases\n- This asymmetry in error modes is the foundation for their complementarity as a verification ensemble\n\n**Cross-reference**: Verified in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/report/paper_consistency_audit.md`\n\n---\n\n### 2. ORACLE ENSEMBLE 90.63% RESULT\n\n**Source**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/data/error_overlap_analysis.txt` and `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/data/cls_cwm_error_overlap.md`\n\n**Complete Error Overlap Statistics (seed42, n=1890)**:\n| Category | Count | Percentage |\n|----------|-------|-----------|\n| Both correct | 1601 | 84.71% |\n| CLS-only correct | 59 | 3.12% |\n| CWM-only correct | 53 | 2.80% |\n| Both wrong | 177 | 9.37% |\n\n**Oracle ensemble accuracy: 90.63%**\n- Union correct: 1713 samples\n- Oracle gain over CLS: +2.80pp\n- Oracle gain over CWM: +3.12pp\n- Cohen's Kappa (predictions): 0.88 (strong agreement)\n- Cohen's Kappa (correctness): 0.73\n\n**Per-mutation complementarity**:\n- off_by_one: Most complementary (CWM-only 4.8%, both wrong 14.9%)\n- return_value: Least complementary (96.8% both correct)\n\n---\n\n### 3. MATCHED-SEED-8B-PREDICTIONS EXPERIMENT\n\n**Source**: Checkpoints dated 2026-05-12 at `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/checkpoints/matched-seed-8b-predictions_DONE_20260512T174621.json`\n\n**Experiment Status**: COMPLETED\n- **Hypothesis**: Generate matched-seed per-instance predictions (8B CWM eval JSONs or 4B supplementary analysis) for error overlap/oracle analysis\n- **Available matched CLS-CWM pairs**: 3 pairs (seed0/seed42/seed456)\n  - CWM seed0: 87.57%\n  - CWM seed42: ~87% (established)\n  - CWM seed456: 86.98%\n- **Missing**: CWM seed123/789 and 8B predictions (distributed across cloud infrastructure)\n- **Conclusion**: 3 pairs sufficient for error overlap analysis; foundational for oracle 90.63% result\n\n---\n\n### 4. EFFICIENCY ANALYSIS (1-Token vs N-Token)\n\n**Source**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/_project/data/inference_cost_results_summary.txt` and worker result JSON\n\n**Inference Cost Comparison** (CPU bfloat16, Qwen3-4B + LoRA):\n\n| Metric | Classification (1-token) | CWM Generation (N-token) | Ratio |\n|--------|------------------------|------------------------|-------|\n| Output tokens (mean) | 2.0 | 6.2 | **3.1x** |\n| Latency (mean) | 9,761 ms | 10,612 ms | **1.09x** |\n| Throughput | 0.1024 sps | 0.0942 sps | 0.92x |\n\n**CWM Target Token Distribution** (1890 samples):\n- Mean: 4.7 tokens\n- Median: 5.0 tokens\n- p95: 7 tokens\n- Max: 28 tokens\n\n**Key Efficiency Insights**:\n1. **Token overhead**: CWM outputs 3.1x more tokens than classification\n2. **CPU latency**: Only 1.09x slower due to prefill dominance (input processing ~260 tokens shared across both methods)\n3. **GPU impact**: Differential will be more pronounced on GPU since per-token decode becomes the bottleneck\n4. **Architectural advantage**: CLS produces exactly 1 token regardless of output complexity; CWM scales with output length\n\n---\n\n### 5. ADDITIONAL KEY FINDINGS\n\n**Paper Statistics Summary** (from `paper_materials.md`):\n- **4B Function-Level**: CLS mean 88.43%, CWM mean 87.19% (gap: +1.25pp)\n- **8B Function-Level**: CLS mean 89.40%, CWM mean 86.96% (gap: +2.43pp)\n- **Scaling gap widening**: Gap increases with model size (+1.18pp from 4B to 8B)\n- **Repo-Level Results**: CLS 83.63% vs CWM 58.04% (25.59pp gap)\n  - CWM failure driver: 53.7–67.2% unparseable (token-budget exhaustion, string-value errors)\n\n**Block Correlation & Clustering**:\n- ICC: 0.191 (significant block structure)\n- Design effect: 3.97x (cluster correlation matters)\n- Error clustering observed: 2.81x more all-correct problems than random expectation\n\n**Paper Material Completeness**:\n- Verified against registry: 88.43/87.19 (5-seed), 2.43pp (3-seed 8B), TOST p=0.007, oracle 90.63%, 83.63/58.04 (repo-level)\n- 42–43% parseable, 53.7–67.2% unparseable (repo-level CWM)\n\n---\n\n### File Locations Reference\n\n| Analysis | Primary File |\n|----------|-------------|\n| Error complementarity (75%/83%) | `/artifacts/_project/report/paper_materials.md` (lines 151-155) |\n| Oracle 90.63% detailed breakdown | `/artifacts/_project/data/error_overlap_analysis.txt` |\n| Matched-seed experiment metadata | `/checkpoints/matched-seed-8b-predictions_DONE_20260512T174621.json` |\n| Inference cost comparison | `/artifacts/_project/data/inference_cost_results_summary.txt` |\n| Complete consistency audit | `/artifacts/_project/report/paper_consistency_audit.md` |\n| CLS vs CWM error overlap detailed | `/artifacts/_project/data/cls_cwm_error_overlap.md` |\n\nAll results are from completed experiments between 2026-05-11 and 2026-05-12, verified against the project registry and cross-referenced in multiple audit reports."}],"totalDurationMs":43291,"totalTokens":60624,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3791,"cache_read_input_tokens":54914,"output_tokens":1913,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3791},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1913,"cache_read_input_tokens":54914,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3791,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":7,"bashCount":5,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
